sub1:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-petroff-kahng-second-assessor-audit-kahng-coral-geometry-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Kahng, Odle & Wakeman (2024) Reef-Coral Colony Geometry & Surface-Area Productivity — MorphoEval overall 49.1/100" ;
        rdfs:comment "Blinded second-assessor pass. The script encodes Kahng, Odle & Wakeman's (2024) accounting rule — skeleton volume grows by G*S/rho per step — and derives, for four idealised shapes (hemisphere, fixed-aspect cone, fixed-thickness disc, fixed-radius cylinder), the one-step linear extension and surface-area productivity (dS/S). The algebra for V(t+1) -> size(t+1) is correct for every shape, and the qualitative conclusions match the paper. However, the script's annual forward-Euler step makes hemisphere extension look size-dependent (0.52 cm/yr at r = 0.5 cm rising to 1.25 cm/yr), whereas the continuous geometry gives C = G/rho at every size; the 'equal G, rho' comparison applies G = 1.5 g cm^-2 yr^-1 to a 0.5 cm plate (yielding 26 cm/yr extension at r = 30 cm and S ~ 10^9 cm^2 after 15 years in the GIF); and no measured coral growth data are compared with the model output. Overall 49.1/100 (faithfulness 42.9, reproducibility 63.7; model-implementation 64.0/100, biological-validation 27.0/100, applicable-only overall 49.1/100; uncalibrated rubric score, not a calibrated probability); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 5564750; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 62, Morphological realism / specimen match 30, Parameter expressivity 68, Morphometric validation 22, Source and data traceability 68, Code-to-model traceability 58, Reproducibility package 64. Output judged: kahng_coral_geometry_morphospace.png: rendered output of 2024-kahng-coral-geometry.py at 5564750, image/png, 282553 B, 1774×1267 px, artifact_sha256 fa8ce6cd95b493eee42054724462d8d7e6380dd161cc7899a464457cd765f812 (sha256 fa8ce6cd95b493eee42054724462d8d7e6380dd161cc7899a464457cd765f812), spec_fingerprint 833cc6f3d6f3988fa15a852dd8366b15c68ef56d6fd98635b3250ff241f4746a. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 833cc6f3d6f3988fa15a852dd8366b15c68ef56d6fd98635b3250ff241f4746a; artifact_sha256: fa8ce6cd95b493eee42054724462d8d7e6380dd161cc7899a464457cd765f812." ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-kahng-coral-geometry> ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 2024-kahng-coral-geometry.py:57-59 — Vendor empirical coral extension/calcification tables from Lough (2008), Hughes (1987), and Kahng (2023) in datasets/kahng/ with full DOIs and SHA-256 digests, and compare model C and SAP against observed colony growth.",
            "remediation needed: 2024-kahng-coral-geometry.py:60,160-178 — Use biologically realistic DISC parameters in panel (c) so a 0.5 cm plate does not extend at 26 cm/yr and obscure the hemisphere and cone curves.",
            "remediation needed: 2024-kahng-coral-geometry.py:68-110,173-182 — Separate continuous differential rates (hemisphere dr/dt = G/rho identically; cone dh/dt = G*sqrt(1+alpha^2)/rho; disc dr/dt = G*r/(2*rho*h)) from the discrete 1-yr Euler step, and expose dt as a parameter." ;
        pk:hasProbability "0.491"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-kahng-coral-geometry> rdfs:label "Kahng, Odle & Wakeman (2024) Reef-Coral Colony Geometry & Surface-Area Productivity faithfully reproduces Scleractinian reef corals (massive Porites, branching Acropora, plating Leptoseris) morphology" ;
        dcterms:identifier "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Claude Fable 5.1 (Cursor subagent e65a3d81-92b5-4bb2-941f-4566032cb3cd, blinded second assessor)" .
}

